# ==============================================================================
# 12-Factor Principle: Factor V — Build, Release, Run
# Strictly separate build and run stages.
#
# Why .dockerignore is mandatory for deterministic twelve-factor builds:
# The Build stage converts a pinned source-control revision into an immutable
# executable bundle. Without a strict .dockerignore, host-compiled artifacts
# (bin/, obj/) and developer-local environment files (.env) can leak into the
# Docker build context, causing two severe Factor V & Factor III violations:
#   1. Host-Binary Contamination: Pre-compiled host DLLs or NuGet project.assets.json
#      graphs targeting macOS/Windows paths overwrite or short-circuit clean
#      Alpine Linux compilation inside the SDK container.
#   2. Credential & Environment Leakage: Local .env files, IDE user settings, or
#      git metadata could be baked permanently into immutable container layers.
# ==============================================================================

# Host compilation outputs and intermediate MSBuild state
**/bin/
**/obj/
TestResults/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# Local environment secrets and overrides (Factor III & Factor V)
.env
.env.*
*.pfx
*.key

# Version control, IDE caches, and OS metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.userosscache
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.DotSettings.user
*.VisualState.xml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Non-workload repository directories not required by container builds
docs/
deploy/
scripts/
tests/
docker-compose*.yml
*.md
